> >a DL for every 2 char levels.
>
> That's _very_ stupid. Monster difficulty is the average of DL and XL;
> lingering on cleared levels and gaining XL is just about the worst thing
> you can do.

When your DL exceeds your XL, the monster difficulty will be greater
than your XL, which means you're in for a tough fight but gain exp
faster.  When your DL is less than your XL, the monster difficulty will
also be less--an easier fight but slower progression.  It's a matter of
style, and I think mine is conservative.  I agree I shouldn't have
stated it in a way that could be interpreted as a "rule", because once
you have a decent AC the game gets easier.  The key point, as you and
others said, is "get better equipment and get it fast".



